=== find-tape help ===
bp3 harness find-tape - InitRecord-first tape lookup:
bp3 harness find-tape --run-id <id> [--entry <id>] [--before-entries <n>] [--after-entries <n>]
bp3 harness find-tape --session-id <id>
Run-id is the sole primary key; --session-id is a reverse lookup that must resolve to exactly one run-id. Both, neither, or disagreeing identity flags are E_USAGE; misses are E_NOT_FOUND; ambiguity is E_AMBIGUOUS and names every candidate. A tape named by an InitRecord or a binding row wins over any scan; when a scan finds several referencing tapes, only tapes carrying the Run's own engine-fsm-edge invocation (BP3_RUN_ID bound to its bp3 q ... u <exp> <engine-fsm-edge> call, engine-fsm-edge from the run-id, exp from the InitRecord) can resolve, and among them the earliest session started at-or-after the Run's InitRecord wins; a tie or none is E_AMBIGUOUS.
--entry returns the one digest-verified entry (sha256 over its exact line, with byte range), widened by --before-entries/--after-entries (non-negative integers, default 0).
Emits {ok, run_id, harness, session_id, wal, pid} or, with --entry, plus {entry, entries}.
Example: bp3 harness find-tape --run-id 20261115T000000Z-handoff-pi-model-c1
